## Decision Task

This is an imitation task, not tactical optimization. Jointly analyze the complete current rally, every missed and successful case, and the style-shift instruction.

First synthesize the missed-shot evidence with the current positions and incoming shot to decide whether the player can produce a legal return into the opponent's court. If not, output `Missed shot`. If an effective return is possible, synthesize all successful cases and apply the style shift only when the evidence supports it. Do not reduce this decision to a comparison of the two nearest cases.

---

## Output Format

Return only one valid JSON object. Do not use markdown fences, XML tags, or text outside the JSON object.

{
  "rationale": "a concise imitation rationale that synthesizes the current rally, all similar cases, and the following instruction",
  "action": {
    "shot_type": "<exact shot type name>",
    "landing_area": <semantic area name string or null>,
    "landing_x": <integer 0 to 354 or null>,
    "landing_y": <integer 0 to 479 or null>,
    "moving_area": <semantic area name string or null>,
    "moving_x": <integer 0 to 354 or null>,
    "moving_y": <integer 0 to 479 or null>
  }
}

## Action Constraints

- `shot_type` must be one of the exact shot type names mentioned above.
- In a serve situation, `shot_type` must be either `Serve short` or `Serve long`.
- Use Missed shot when the agent fails to reach the shuttle, the physical situation or positioning is too difficult to produce any legal return into the opponent's court.
- For `Missed shot`, set both semantic areas and all four coordinates to `null`.
- For every other shot, all coordinates must be integers in the valid grid and match their semantic areas.
- Do not include extra fields.
